! =============================================================================
! Manual Tutorial Problem #11, adapted: FLiNaK eutectic temperature
! =============================================================================
! FLiNaK is the ternary eutectic 46.5 LiF - 11.5 NaF - 42 KF (mol%), widely
! considered as an MSR coolant/carrier salt for its low melting point.
! Composition converted to elements: Li=46.5, Na=11.5, K=42.0, F=100.0 mol.
!
! Note on database: the manual's Tutorial #11 uses the export-controlled
! MSAR_Ver_1.dat (request access from the MSTDB maintainers; see the manual's
! Table 10). This file instead uses the MSTDB V4.1 fluoride database already
! in data/, which contains the same Li-Na-K-F system under a newer
! parameterization -- numbers differ slightly from the manual's listing
! (database version, not a different system).
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/saltfoss/06_flinak_eutectic.ti
! Verified output at 440 C: two solid FM3M (LiF-rich, KF-rich) fluorite-type
! phases plus solid NaF -- i.e. still below the eutectic. Sweep temperature
! (see 06_flinak_sweep.ti) to find the melting point: with this database, the
! transition to a single MSFL liquid falls between 459 C and 459.5 C. The
! manual reports ~470 C with the older database version.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 440
pressure          = 1.0
mass(3)           = 46.5
mass(11)          = 11.5
mass(19)          = 42.0
mass(9)           = 100.0
temperature unit  = C
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MSD-TC_V4.1_Fluorides_No_Func.dat
print mode        = 2
